      "block_id": "1212.0957_p1_b3",
      "text": "Abstract. In this paper, algorithms are developed for computing the\nStirling transform and the inverse Stirling transform; speci\ufb01cally, we\ninvestigate a class of sequences satisfying a two-term recurrence. We\nderive a general identity which generalizes the usual Stirling transform\nand investigate the corresponding generating functions also. In addi-\ntion, some interesting consequences of these results related to classical\nsequences like Fibonacci, Bernoulli and the numbers of derangements\nhave been derived.\n",
      "bbox": [
        162.48,
        208.82,
        449.54,
        294.8
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
