    {
      "block_id": "1212.0957_p1_b5",
      "text": "The Stirling numbers arise frequently in mathematics, especially in enu-\nmerative problems. This is the reason of their important role in combina-\ntorial analysis, number theory, probability, graph theory, calculus of \ufb01nite\ndi\ufb00erences and interpolation. The notations for these numbers have never\nbeen standardized, this paper follows the notation of Riordan for the signed\nStirling numbers of the \ufb01rst kind s (n, k) and Knuth\u2019s notation for the Stir-\nling numbers of the second kind\n",
      "bbox": [
