      "block_id": "1212.0957_p1_b23",
      "text": "The identity (1.1) has a combinatorial interpretation given in [2]. If an\nis the number of objects in some class with points labeled 1, 2, . . . , n (with\nall labels distinct) then bn is the number of objects with points labeled\n1, 2, . . . , n (with repetitions allowed).\nIn this paper, algorithms are developed for computing the Stirling trans-\nform and the inverse Stirling transform; speci\ufb01cally, we investigate a class\nof sequences satisfying a two-term recurrence. We derive a general identity\n",
